    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d260">

                <pb facs="0230" n="220" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg220"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/4–149: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Peiping</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Clubb</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-04-01">April 1,
                        1949</date>.<lb/>[Received April 2—5:38 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>541. ReContel 525, March 31. <hi rendition="#italic">Hsin Min Pao</hi> today
                    carried following item regarding cruiser <hi rendition="#italic">Chungking:</hi>
                </p>
                <pb facs="0231" n="221" xml:id="pg221"/>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“Under leadership Commander Teng Chao-hsiang, warship <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Chungking</hi>, largest cruiser of Kuomintang reactionary navy,
                        revolted February 25 and joined battle camp of People’s forces. But Chiang
                        Kai-shek, public enemy of the people, in collusion with the most fiendish
                        and wicked American imperialist clique, who have determined to be enemy of
                        Chinese people, sent air planes to Hulutao to bomb and sink cruiser <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chungking</hi> on 4 consecutive days, March 17, 18,
                        19 and 20.</p>
                    <p>Upon hearing news all Chinese without exception were infuriated. They
                        recognize that diabolical mien of American imperialists, the masters of
                        bandit Chiang Kai-shek, has now been quite exposed; the following is letter
                        written by group of primary school students:</p>
                </quote>
                <p>. . . . . . .</p>
                <p>Sent Department 541, Nanking 334, Office Embassy Canton, Shanghai 374, Tsingtao,
                    by mail to Tientsin.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clubb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
